capability read-api-host-configuration
intent: The settings the hosting facade acts on, declared with the host's other declarations, so a change to one is a re-declaration and a new pin and never a change to the facade or to host data it interprets. The facade invokes it once, before it binds its port, and holds the answer for as long as it runs; a refusal or a failed delivery stops the host. It answers: the envelope each request is handed to serve-http-request in, the raw request going in as the envelope request's input; how long a request waits for a free request kernel (2 s: App Service stops a request at 230 s, and the facade waits up to 228 s for a request kernel's answer) and the response that refuses it past that wait; the response for a delivery that answers none and for a directive the facade cannot carry out; for runs, the most events a run keeps and the largest observation kept whole (both read by project-api-run-events), the bounds of a trace chunk, how many admitted runs may wait for a worker, with the response that refuses a run past that bound and the delivery answer that run then ends with, and how many ended runs the facade keeps for reconnects until a run's stream replays its retained trace; how often a quiet stream is kept alive; for the estate live observation channel, the capability that publishes it, the frames and bytes it retains, the events and bytes it publishes in one batch, and whether request executions are published, which they are not; the drawing read, its interval and its page of changes; and the kernel's observation queue bounds, null because nothing sets them, so the kernel's defaults hold (512 records, 1 MiB, a 2000 ms drain). Every response is complete as declared, its Content-Length the byte count of its body, and the facade writes it unchanged.
outcome: api-host-configuration.v1: the hosting facade's declared settings
inquiry: What does the hosting facade act on?
input contract read-api-host-configuration-request.v1 {"type":"object"}
output contract api-host-configuration.v1 {"type":"object","required":["contractId","request","runs","streams","channel","drawings","observationQueue"]}
cli display outcome as json
scenario read-api-host-configuration root terminal
given: the hosting facade starting
when: the declared settings are read
then: the outcome is the facade's declared settings
operation read-api-host-configuration.answer kind invoke-port port read-api-host-configuration-answer
platform bind read-api-host-configuration-answer
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
config: {"expression":{"op":"literal","value":{"contractId":"api-host-configuration.v1","request":{"envelope":{"deliveryType":"sfx-command-delivery.v1","operation":"invoke","request":{"object":"capability","verb":"invoke","subject":"serve-http-request","inputType":"text"}},"waitMilliseconds":2000,"busy":"HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable\r\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\r\nContent-Length: 40\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n{\"error\":{\"code\":\"REQUEST_KERNEL_BUSY\"}}","failure":"HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway\r\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\r\nContent-Length: 43\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n{\"error\":{\"code\":\"KERNEL_DELIVERY_FAILED\"}}"},"runs":{"events":{"maxEvents":50000,"wholeObservationBytes":1048576},"trace":{"chunkBytes":524288,"chunkEvents":2000},"queue":{"waiting":64,"refusal":"HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable\r\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\r\nContent-Length: 35\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n{\"error\":{\"code\":\"RUN_QUEUE_FULL\"}}","delivery":{"disposition":"failed","error":{"code":"RUN_QUEUE_FULL"}}},"retainedEnded":64},"streams":{"keepaliveMilliseconds":15000},"channel":{"publish":{"capabilityId":"publish-estate-live-observation"},"retainedFrames":20000,"retainedBytes":33554432,"batchEvents":200,"batchBytes":1048576,"requests":{"published":false}},"drawings":{"capabilityId":"read-estate-drawing-changes","intervalMilliseconds":2000,"limit":20},"observationQueue":null}}}
